  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0396' comprises seven tables. The primary function of this schema is to manage user profiles, travel guides, restaurant information, hotel details, scenic spots, routes, and user-written guides.\nThe User_Table represents user profiles. It contains columns for 'Nickname', 'Password', 'Profile_Picture', and 'Username', all of which are VARCHAR(255) data types. The 'Username' column is the primary key, ensuring entity integrity as it uniquely identifies each user.\nThe Guide_Table stores travel guides. It has columns for 'Category', 'Content', 'Guide_Title', and 'Tags', all of which are VARCHAR(255) data types. The 'Guide_Title' is the primary key, ensuring entity integrity.\nThe Restaurant_Table contains information about restaurants. It has columns for 'Image', 'Introduction', 'Location', and 'Restaurant_Name', all of which are VARCHAR(255) data types. The 'Restaurant_Name' is the primary key, ensuring entity integrity.\nThe Hotel_Table stores hotel details. It has columns for 'Hotel_Name', 'Image', 'Introduction', and 'Location', all of which are VARCHAR(255) data types. The 'Hotel_Name' is the primary key, ensuring entity integrity.\nThe Scenic_Spot_Table stores information about scenic spots. It has columns for 'Address', 'Days', 'Image', 'Introduction', 'Opening_Hours', 'Scenic_Spot_Name', and 'Tips', all of which are VARCHAR(255) data types. The 'Scenic_Spot_Name' is the primary key, ensuring entity integrity.\nThe Route table contains information about travel routes. It has columns for 'Content', 'Introduction', 'Route_Name', and 'Tags', all of which are VARCHAR(255) data types. The 'Route_Name' is the primary key, ensuring entity integrity.\nThe Write_Guide_Table is a junction table that links users to their written guides. It has columns for 'Guide_Title' and 'Username', both of which are VARCHAR(255) data types. Both columns are primary keys, ensuring entity integrity. The 'Guide_Title' and 'Username' columns are foreign keys referencing the 'Guide_Table' and 'User_Table', respectively, ensuring referential integrity.\nThis schema is exhaustive but should be readable to a non-expert.",
  "gold_question": "The main functions of a certain tourism information management system include:\n1. User management: including the management of user names, passwords, avatars, nicknames and other information. Users can write guides.\n2. Guide management: including the management of guide titles, categories, tags, content and other information.\n3. Hotel management: including the management of hotel names, introductions, pictures, locations and other information.\n4. Hotel management: including the management of hotel names, introductions, pictures, locations and other information.\n5. Attraction management: including the management of attraction names, introductions, pictures, addresses, opening hours, tips, days and other information.\n6. Route management: including the management of route names, content, tags, introductions and other information.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0396.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0396\nCREATE TABLE `user_table` (\n  `nickname` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `profile_picture` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`username`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `guide_table` (\n  `category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `guide_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `tags` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`guide_title`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `restaurant_table` (\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `introduction` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `restaurant_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`restaurant_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `hotel_table` (\n  `hotel_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `introduction` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`hotel_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `scenic_spot_table` (\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `days` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `introduction` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `opening_hours` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `scenic_spot_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `tips` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`scenic_spot_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `route_table` (\n  `content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `introduction` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `route_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `tags` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`route_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `write_guide_table` (\n  `guide_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`guide_title`, `username`),\n  CONSTRAINT `write_guide_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`guide_title`) REFERENCES `guide_table` (`guide_title`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `write_guide_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`username`) REFERENCES `user_table` (`username`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
